
This directory is intended for PlatformIO Test Runner and project tests.

Unit Testing is a software testing method by which individual units of
source code, sets of one or more MCU program modules together with associated
control data, usage procedures, and operating procedures, are tested to
determine whether they are fit for use. Unit testing finds problems early
in the development cycle.

More information about PlatformIO Unit Testing:
- https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html


================================================================================
Host tests (no hardware, no ESP32 toolchain)
================================================================================

test/host/ holds two g++ regression tests for the Arduino-independent parts of
src/main.cpp. They compile and run on any machine with g++ (C++17); you do NOT
need a board, PlatformIO, or the ESP32 toolchain to run them.

    bash test/host/run_host_tests.sh

What they guard:

  test_fluidics.cpp   - the fluidic geometry, flow rates, and derived timings
                        (line volumes, base fill, dose, prime/purge/rinse
                        durations). It does NOT copy the constants: the script
                        re-extracts the block from src/main.cpp into
                        geom_block.inc on every run, so the assertions always
                        check the shipped source. Regression guards live here for
                        the two bugs already fixed once - the 35%-vs-100% prime
                        duty error and the 33000 ms overfill - so they cannot
                        silently come back.

  test_colormath.cpp  - the hue/HSV math, branch-cut unwrapping, hue->pH
                        interpolation, and calibration-table validate/parse/
                        upsert logic. These function bodies are MIRRORED from
                        main.cpp (they pull in Arduino types that will not
                        compile on the host), so if you change one of those
                        functions in main.cpp, update its copy here too.

Adding a testable constant: put it in main.cpp BETWEEN the TUBE_ML_PER_CM line
and the `RINSE_DRAIN_MS = DRAIN_MS;` line - that is the range the extractor
copies. Anything outside it is invisible to test_fluidics.

The compiled binaries and the generated geom_block.inc are git-ignored.
